'''Jusuf Muntasir''' is a [[Balisca|Baliscan]] professional wrestler and traditional oil wrestler. He is best known for his background in [[Baliscan oil wrestling|mosaraza]], the traditional national grappling sport of Balisca, and for his debut in [[New Okaiken Pro-Wrestling]] (NOPW) on July 29, 2026, where he interrupted the [[IGO Intercontinental Championship]] match between [[Marcus Vance|Marcus "The Drill" Vance]] and [[Daigo Kuroki]].

== Background ==

Muntasir was raised in the [[Baliscan oil wrestling|mosaraza]] tradition, the close-body oil-wrestling style that developed in [[Balisca]] from Andalusi roots. In mosaraza, competitors wrestle bare-chested in heavy leather trousers called ''quiswa'' or ''kiswa'', covered in oil, with victory achieved through leverage, controlled falls, and grounded dominance rather than striking or submission. The sport is deeply tied to Baliscan rural festivals, harvest celebrations, and public honour.

Before entering professional wrestling, Muntasir competed in the national festival circuit of mosaraza, where he became known for his physical power, low centre of gravity, and contempt for the theatrical elements of modern sport. His approach was traditionalist: he believed that true grappling required no ropes, no predetermined finishes, and no spectacle beyond the contest itself.

== Professional wrestling career ==

=== New Okaiken Pro-Wrestling (2026–present) ===

Muntasir was introduced to NOPW through a Baliscan sporting manager who arranged for him to debut on the [[NOPW Wednesday]] touring product. His arrival was kept secret until the go-home show before the [[Island Invasion Tour]] on July 29, 2026.

During the [[IGO Intercontinental Championship]] match between champion [[Marcus Vance]] and challenger [[Daigo Kuroki]] at [[NOPW Wednesday Episode 6]], Muntasir walked to the ring while the lights were cut. He attacked both Vance and Kuroki without choosing a side, causing the match to end in a no contest. He then took a microphone and declared, in heavily accented Mercian: ''"My name is Jusuf Muntasir. In Balisca, we call this mosaraza. You call it pro wrestling. I call it a lie."''

The debut immediately established Muntasir as an outsider heel with no faction allegiance. Notably, no member of the [[Cannon Club]] — including Vance's own stablemates — came to his aid during the attack, contributing to Vance's growing isolation from the faction and his organic babyface turn.

== In-ring style ==

Muntasir's style is adapted from mosaraza: close-body grappling, heavy leverage through his opponent's clothing or trunks, low stance, powerful throws, and grounded control. He favours clinch work, gutwrench suplexes, and submissions that trap the opponent's arms and legs simultaneously. His presence is methodical and intimidating — he does not rush, and he does not celebrate.

== Appearance ==

Muntasir is a powerfully built heavyweight with dark curly hair, a full beard, and intense dark eyes. His complexion is olive. He typically wears black compression gear with elements of the traditional Baliscan ''quiswa'' — heavy leather strapping around the thighs and waist — blending the traditional oil-wrestling garment with modern professional wrestling attire.

== Finishing moves ==
* '''Abrazo de Terra''' — a grounded body lock / clinch submission, named after the colloquial Baliscan nickname for mosaraza ("ground hug")
* '''Mosaraza Driver''' — a gutwrench powerbomb

